WEBVTT

00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:04.350
Are you really going to 
be okay all by yourself?

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:06.210
I'll be fine.

00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:07.720
If anything happens,

00:00:07.720 --> 00:00:09.900
be sure to contact the 
teacher on night shift.

00:00:10.470 --> 00:00:13.730
And of course you can contact me, too.

00:00:13.730 --> 00:00:15.760
I'll get to you and back home in a jiffy.

00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:17.910
I know. Thank you.

00:00:18.450 --> 00:00:21.010
I made some broth for New Year's soba,

00:00:21.010 --> 00:00:22.600
so be sure to warm it up and eat it later.

00:00:23.010 --> 00:00:25.240
Also, the New Year's food is in the cupboard.

00:00:25.730 --> 00:00:29.050
And when you're eating the mochi, 
make sure you chew it thoroughly.

00:00:29.050 --> 00:00:29.720
Oh, and—

00:00:29.720 --> 00:00:32.180
Senpai, we're gonna miss the train.

00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:35.340
Goodness gracious. 
I'll see you later, Nina-chan.

00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:36.970
Bye-bye, Nina!

00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:39.020
Nina-san, I wish you a happy New Year.

00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:40.850
We'll see you in the new year.

00:00:40.850 --> 00:00:43.730
Let's dream of Mount Fuji, 
a hawk, and white rice!

00:00:43.730 --> 00:00:44.990
See you later.

00:00:59.570 --> 00:01:00.700
It's so quiet.

00:01:02.510 --> 00:01:07.180
Almost like I'm the only person 
in the whole wide world.

00:01:14.540 --> 00:01:19.850
<i>Now I can finally watch all those comedy 
DVDs I've been saving up without reserve.</i>

00:01:19.850 --> 00:01:21.780
<i>And I'll do a solo comedy sketch.</i>

00:01:21.780 --> 00:01:23.350
<i>And a even a solo two-person comedy sketch.</i>

00:01:23.810 --> 00:01:28.140
<i>And then I'll research to my 
heart's content whether or not</i>

00:01:28.140 --> 00:01:30.820
<i>I can use the superstring theory to 
analyze the universe's inflation.</i>

00:01:31.140 --> 00:01:33.820
<i>Freedom is truly happiness.</i>

00:01:34.290 --> 00:01:35.780
Welcome back, Nina-chan!

00:01:38.830 --> 00:01:39.990
What are you doing?

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:42.870
Getting all warm and cozy.

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:44.740
That's not what I mean.

00:01:44.740 --> 00:01:46.500
What are you doing here?

00:01:47.410 --> 00:01:48.960
I thought you were going back home.

00:01:49.970 --> 00:01:50.840
But...

00:01:51.680 --> 00:01:53.800
When I heard you'd be here all alone,

00:01:54.940 --> 00:01:57.360
I thought it'd be more fun to 
spend New Year's Eve together.

00:01:57.360 --> 00:01:57.800
Right?

00:03:24.530 --> 00:03:27.090
Do you want a mikan, too?

00:03:27.090 --> 00:03:28.350
No.

00:03:28.890 --> 00:03:32.290
Okay. Too bad. They're so good.

00:03:32.290 --> 00:03:34.520
And anyway, what is this?

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:36.490
It's called a kotatsu!

00:03:37.620 --> 00:03:39.530
It's all warm and toasty.

00:03:40.300 --> 00:03:42.040
That's not what I mean.

00:03:42.040 --> 00:03:45.160
I'm asking what all of 
this is doing in my room.

00:03:45.160 --> 00:03:46.700
But?

00:03:46.970 --> 00:03:50.540
In Japan, you celebrate the new year by 
getting all toasty under the kotatsu,

00:03:50.540 --> 00:03:53.830
eating mikan, eating New Year's soba,

00:03:54.480 --> 00:03:55.650
watching the NHK Year-End Song Festival,

00:03:55.650 --> 00:04:00.010
eating dried sweet potato, eating 
mochi, eating rice crackers—

00:03:58.400 --> 00:04:00.010
It sounds like nothing but eating.

00:04:00.340 --> 00:04:01.260
Don't worry about it.

00:04:02.400 --> 00:04:04.640
I've got enough for you, too!

00:04:06.320 --> 00:04:09.990
Nina-chan, hurry up and 
get under the kotatsu.

00:04:10.690 --> 00:04:12.770
Kotatsu are amazing, aren't they?

00:04:12.770 --> 00:04:16.440
Karen told me that once you get 
under one, you can never leave.

00:04:17.240 --> 00:04:19.490
And she was right.

00:04:22.600 --> 00:04:24.740
There's no way that's true.

00:04:32.880 --> 00:04:34.080
She was right.

00:04:34.370 --> 00:04:37.500
Right? It makes you feel 
like you never wanna leave.

00:04:39.780 --> 00:04:41.490
Looks like we have visitors.

00:04:41.490 --> 00:04:42.790
Yeah.

00:04:43.570 --> 00:04:45.600
Wonder what they're doing 
out there on New Year's Eve.

00:04:45.600 --> 00:04:46.300
Who knows?

00:04:49.830 --> 00:04:51.560
Nina-chan!

00:04:54.140 --> 00:04:57.240
I know, right? Belle, can you get it?

00:04:58.120 --> 00:04:59.680
I guess we've got no choice now.

00:04:59.680 --> 00:05:01.360
We're going to have to have a contest,

00:05:01.360 --> 00:05:03.030
and the loser has to get the door.

00:05:03.520 --> 00:05:05.150
What kind of contest?

00:05:05.150 --> 00:05:06.320
Rock-paper-scissors?

00:05:06.320 --> 00:05:08.850
<i>I don't feel like I'll 
win by relying on luck.</i>

00:05:08.850 --> 00:05:10.690
A-A staring contest.

00:05:10.690 --> 00:05:11.830
Sure.

00:05:12.730 --> 00:05:14.690
Let's having a staring contest.

00:05:14.690 --> 00:05:16.540
No laughing!

00:05:16.540 --> 00:05:18.240
Ready, set, go!

00:05:19.750 --> 00:05:22.760
Nina-chan, that's way too funny!

00:05:24.360 --> 00:05:26.680
Aw, I lost.

00:05:28.880 --> 00:05:31.010
Was I that funny?

00:05:33.540 --> 00:05:35.720
You don't have to laugh that much.

00:05:39.940 --> 00:05:41.370
Nina-chan!

00:05:43.060 --> 00:05:45.180
Tetra-Heaven-Class Deliciousness!

00:05:43.540 --> 00:05:45.190
I got some crab!

00:05:56.800 --> 00:05:58.300
Delicious, right?

00:05:58.300 --> 00:06:00.100
Yeah. It's delicious.

00:06:08.090 --> 00:06:11.790
Oh, yeah. Who gave you the crab?

00:06:11.790 --> 00:06:14.430
I dunno. I didn't know the person.

00:06:15.740 --> 00:06:18.310
I wonder who it was?

00:06:17.980 --> 00:06:20.020
Name:  Rino Fujisaki

00:06:17.980 --> 00:06:20.020
Note:         Must arrive by the 31st

00:06:25.660 --> 00:06:27.090
Still?

00:06:27.090 --> 00:06:29.090
Huh? What?

00:06:29.090 --> 00:06:31.350
Honestly?

00:06:33.700 --> 00:06:35.120
Here we are!

00:06:35.490 --> 00:06:37.000
Did you invite someone over?

00:06:37.380 --> 00:06:40.750
To tell the truth, just for you,

00:06:40.750 --> 00:06:44.580
I ordered the absolute top quality 
red king crab for our hot pot.

00:06:44.580 --> 00:06:46.850
It's New Year's Eve, after all.

00:06:46.850 --> 00:06:49.400
Gotta splurge a bit!

00:06:51.260 --> 00:06:52.390
Everything okay?

00:06:52.390 --> 00:06:54.640
Sorry

00:06:55.300 --> 00:06:57.640
Is it because the delivery was late?

00:06:57.940 --> 00:07:03.340
Well then, time to taste 
what the best has to offer.

00:07:03.340 --> 00:07:04.450
Delicious!

00:07:04.450 --> 00:07:06.150
That's kind of a weird crab.

00:07:06.150 --> 00:07:08.400
It's the taste that's top quality!

00:07:08.970 --> 00:07:11.640
Take a closer look. They're top quality!

00:07:11.640 --> 00:07:12.740
Let's see.

00:07:13.870 --> 00:07:15.070
Well it does taste like crab.

00:07:15.070 --> 00:07:17.340
Top quality!

00:07:16.580 --> 00:07:19.020
Marine Blue Crab Sticks

00:07:23.570 --> 00:07:26.800
Lion, I don't think crab 
sticks are going to cut it.

00:07:26.800 --> 00:07:29.180
But crab sticks are delicious!

00:07:32.390 --> 00:07:34.580
It's almost midnight!

00:07:34.580 --> 00:07:36.260
We've gotta eat the New Year's soba!

00:07:40.020 --> 00:07:43.020
Red           White

00:07:41.490 --> 00:07:43.330
Thanks for the food!

00:07:45.620 --> 00:07:47.270
Isn't it delicious?

00:07:47.270 --> 00:07:49.780
Japan's New Year's Eve has lots of yummy food, huh?

00:07:50.050 --> 00:07:51.300
You're right.

00:07:51.920 --> 00:07:55.210
I think we should properly apologize about 
what happened with the crab later after all.

00:07:55.210 --> 00:07:56.030
Sure!

00:07:56.500 --> 00:07:58.410
Let's catch a crab and bring it to them!

00:07:59.520 --> 00:08:01.280
Let's just buy one.

00:08:01.280 --> 00:08:02.920
We can get one for Yuko-senpai, too.

00:08:03.700 --> 00:08:04.990
You're right.

00:08:04.990 --> 00:08:08.050
We should get some new crab sticks for her!

00:08:13.050 --> 00:08:14.760
It's the New Year's Eve bell!

00:08:14.760 --> 00:08:15.760
You're right.

00:08:16.770 --> 00:08:18.890
Nina-chan, did you know?

00:08:19.170 --> 00:08:21.560
Why everyone eats soba on New Year's Eve?

00:08:21.560 --> 00:08:22.390
Why?

00:08:22.820 --> 00:08:25.020
Yayoi-chan taught me.

00:08:25.690 --> 00:08:29.170
Soba is easier to cut than other noodles.

00:08:29.170 --> 00:08:32.440
So it symbolizes how you can "cut off" 
the hardships of the previous year.

00:08:33.120 --> 00:08:37.220
"And we should all be grateful that we 
may face the new year safe and sound."

00:08:37.220 --> 00:08:37.950
So she says!

00:08:39.780 --> 00:08:42.080
Thanks for everything this year.

00:08:45.290 --> 00:08:46.080
Delicious!

00:08:48.630 --> 00:08:50.110
We should be grateful, huh?

00:08:51.530 --> 00:08:52.870
Thank you.

00:09:12.190 --> 00:09:13.790
It's finally time.

00:09:13.790 --> 00:09:14.570
Yeah.

00:09:15.120 --> 00:09:17.410
This year was really fun,

00:09:17.410 --> 00:09:19.070
so it's kinda sad seeing it come to an end.

00:09:19.720 --> 00:09:22.410
I'm sure next year will be a good one, too.

00:09:22.410 --> 00:09:23.330
You think?

00:09:24.390 --> 00:09:25.830
I'm sure.

00:09:27.010 --> 00:09:28.150
I'm so happy.

00:09:28.150 --> 00:09:31.710
I never thought I could ring in 
the new year with you, Nina-chan.

00:09:34.400 --> 00:09:36.150
Lion, are you cold?

00:09:36.150 --> 00:09:37.830
No, I'm okay.

00:09:37.830 --> 00:09:39.890
<i>There's only a short 
while until the new year.</i>

00:09:38.870 --> 00:09:39.890
Do you want to wear this?

00:09:40.600 --> 00:09:41.000
Here.

00:09:41.000 --> 00:09:41.390
<i>Five.</i>

00:09:42.120 --> 00:09:43.170
<i>Four.</i>

00:09:43.170 --> 00:09:44.290
<i>Three.</i>

00:09:43.170 --> 00:09:44.290
Nina-chan.

00:09:44.290 --> 00:09:45.290
<i>Two.</i>

00:09:45.290 --> 00:09:45.890
<i>One.</i>

00:09:47.510 --> 00:09:50.070
<i>Happy New Year, everyone!</i>

00:09:58.450 --> 00:10:00.180
Was that just...?

00:10:00.180 --> 00:10:01.860
You've never done that before?

00:10:02.450 --> 00:10:03.390
Back at home,

00:10:03.390 --> 00:10:07.710
we kiss the person we like the most 
right when the new year comes.

00:10:08.280 --> 00:10:10.890
Happy New Year, Nina-chan.

00:10:10.890 --> 00:10:12.860
Looking forward to another year with you!

00:10:12.860 --> 00:10:15.210
M-Me too.

00:10:18.290 --> 00:10:19.680
Belle!

00:10:20.020 --> 00:10:21.820
Happy New Year to you, too, Belle!

00:10:26.440 --> 00:10:27.480
Gosh.

00:10:28.110 --> 00:10:29.840
And that was my first time.

00:10:29.980 --> 00:10:32.980
Episode 11

00:10:29.980 --> 00:10:32.980
The Countdown is the Time
 To Plan Your Year Around

00:10:35.360 --> 00:10:38.340
Great! It looks like I've got 
just enough for everyone.

00:10:39.380 --> 00:10:42.490
I can smell the sweet smell of chocolate!

00:10:42.860 --> 00:10:44.740
Woah! There's lots!

00:10:45.130 --> 00:10:47.040
Are these chocolates for Valentine's Day?

00:10:47.040 --> 00:10:50.250
Yes. I decided to try 
chocolate cupcakes this year.

00:10:50.650 --> 00:10:53.250
I went for something healthy 
and low in calories.

00:10:54.530 --> 00:10:56.720
Thank you, Yuko-senpai!

00:10:56.720 --> 00:10:58.010
It looks delicious.

00:10:58.360 --> 00:11:00.830
I'd like you to have one too, Yayoi-chan.

00:11:00.830 --> 00:11:02.500
Happy Valentine's.

00:11:03.400 --> 00:11:05.510
It's absolutely adorable.

00:11:05.510 --> 00:11:08.210
Thank you very much, Yuko-senpai.

00:11:08.210 --> 00:11:09.400
Goodness gracious.

00:11:09.400 --> 00:11:12.980
Just seeing you that happy fills me with joy.

00:11:14.200 --> 00:11:16.790
What's the matter, Lion-san?

00:11:16.790 --> 00:11:19.150
I wanted to do something like this, too.

00:11:19.150 --> 00:11:23.070
I wanted to give Nina-chan 
Valentine's chocolate.

00:11:23.070 --> 00:11:24.510
Lion-san...

00:11:25.200 --> 00:11:26.490
There's still time!

00:11:27.470 --> 00:11:28.940
All the ingredients are here,

00:11:28.940 --> 00:11:31.210
so how about we make some 
together, Lion-chan?

00:11:31.210 --> 00:11:32.370
Really?

00:11:32.660 --> 00:11:33.920
Of course!

00:11:33.920 --> 00:11:37.880
Excuse me, but would you mind 
if I participate as well?

00:11:37.880 --> 00:11:41.040
I've always wanted to try 
making chocolate by hand.

00:11:41.040 --> 00:11:42.880
We'd be happy to have you.

00:11:52.600 --> 00:11:54.040
All done.

00:11:54.040 --> 00:11:55.020
Me too!

00:11:55.540 --> 00:11:58.870
Goodness gracious, you're both amazing cooks.

00:12:01.040 --> 00:12:03.700
To make the outside have 
just the right crunch,

00:12:04.280 --> 00:12:06.360
we'll set the oven to 200 degrees,

00:12:06.360 --> 00:12:07.700
and bake for 20 minutes.

00:12:07.700 --> 00:12:11.710
Time

00:12:07.700 --> 00:12:11.710
Temperature

00:12:08.140 --> 00:12:11.710
20 degrees, and 200 minutes.

00:12:11.980 --> 00:12:13.540
It's the opposite, Lion-san!

00:12:13.540 --> 00:12:15.400
Huh? The opposite?

00:12:16.810 --> 00:12:18.840
W-What do I do?

00:12:21.170 --> 00:12:23.470
Start

00:12:22.370 --> 00:12:23.470
This is a problem.

00:12:24.580 --> 00:12:27.810
It looks like Mr. Oven is 
not in the best of moods.

00:12:27.810 --> 00:12:30.660
I'm sorry. It's all my fault.

00:12:30.660 --> 00:12:32.380
It's not your fault, Lion-chan.

00:12:32.380 --> 00:12:34.710
That's right. Don't let it get to you!

00:12:35.680 --> 00:12:38.800
But now we won't be able 
to bake our chocolate.

00:12:38.800 --> 00:12:40.800
And without chocolate...

00:12:40.800 --> 00:12:42.990
<i>I'm so happy. Thank you.</i>

00:12:43.320 --> 00:12:45.240
My day of love will never come.

00:12:45.920 --> 00:12:47.860
Don't worry, Lion-chan.

00:12:47.860 --> 00:12:49.860
If we ask Mahiro-chan,

00:12:49.860 --> 00:12:51.870
I'm sure she'll be able to fix it.

00:12:54.440 --> 00:12:56.980
Mahiro-chan, do you think you can fix it?

00:12:56.980 --> 00:12:58.250
No problem.

00:12:58.760 --> 00:13:01.420
Just in time for me to test out a new 
invention I wanted to put into action.

00:13:01.420 --> 00:13:02.380
I call it:

00:13:02.380 --> 00:13:06.640
The "I'll Fix Anything! 
Leave It To Me! Number 3."

00:13:08.590 --> 00:13:11.700
<i>Destroy. Destroy.</i>

00:13:11.700 --> 00:13:12.990
<i>Destroy.</i>

00:13:12.990 --> 00:13:14.390
All done!

00:13:17.660 --> 00:13:19.700
What in the world did you do?

00:13:19.700 --> 00:13:21.470
That's strange.

00:13:21.470 --> 00:13:24.650
According to my calculations, the 
voltage should really keep it in check.

00:13:26.000 --> 00:13:29.030
Huh? It looks like it's 
clanking around even more now!

00:13:30.130 --> 00:13:31.980
Lion-chan, look out!

00:13:40.140 --> 00:13:41.670
Nina-chan!

00:13:43.190 --> 00:13:44.710
You're so cool!

00:13:45.400 --> 00:13:47.960
You don't look like someone 
who was in a desperate situation

00:13:47.960 --> 00:13:50.290
just one second ago.

00:13:53.900 --> 00:13:56.160
They've baked through completely.

00:13:56.160 --> 00:13:57.420
So we can eat them?

00:13:57.420 --> 00:13:59.350
Yes, it should be fine.

00:14:01.450 --> 00:14:03.240
It's Valentine's chocolate.

00:14:03.240 --> 00:14:05.520
Nina-chan, thank you for everything.

00:14:05.520 --> 00:14:07.990
You too. Thank you.

00:14:08.700 --> 00:14:10.950
Should I eat it right now?

00:14:10.950 --> 00:14:11.990
Yup!

00:14:12.300 --> 00:14:13.700
Here it goes.

00:14:19.450 --> 00:14:20.380
It's delicious.

00:14:20.380 --> 00:14:22.630
Yay! I did it!

00:14:22.630 --> 00:14:24.930
I'm so happy for you, Lion-chan.

00:14:24.930 --> 00:14:28.180
It's all thanks to all the hard 
work "Leave It To Me! Number 3" did!

00:14:28.180 --> 00:14:31.470
Hard work? I believe you mean trouble.

00:14:31.780 --> 00:14:34.630
Yayoi-chan, who are you going 
to give your chocolate to?

00:14:34.630 --> 00:14:36.410
Karin and Karen.

00:14:36.410 --> 00:14:39.100
They have always been there to support me.

00:14:39.800 --> 00:14:41.730
I can think of no one else 
I'm more grateful towards.

00:14:44.500 --> 00:14:45.770
Nina-chan?

00:14:47.150 --> 00:14:48.990
Nina-chan, are you all right?

00:14:49.360 --> 00:14:51.740
Your face is a bit red.

00:14:52.130 --> 00:14:53.620
Nina-chan?

00:14:56.950 --> 00:14:57.910
Lion,

00:14:59.020 --> 00:15:00.170
I love you.

00:15:06.560 --> 00:15:10.110
Um... Nina-chan?

00:15:10.110 --> 00:15:11.270
Lion.

00:15:14.230 --> 00:15:14.970
I love you.

00:15:18.960 --> 00:15:22.110
She's completely different from usual.

00:15:22.110 --> 00:15:23.680
What in the world happened?

00:15:23.680 --> 00:15:25.710
I think we probably have Amol,

00:15:25.710 --> 00:15:27.230
or the arrow of Cupid, to thank for this.

00:15:27.230 --> 00:15:28.990
The arrow of Cupid?

00:15:31.240 --> 00:15:34.160
Running Theories with Mahirun

00:15:32.160 --> 00:15:34.160
<i>Running Theories with Mahirun!</i>

00:15:34.160 --> 00:15:35.780
Today's explanation with Mahirun!

00:15:34.550 --> 00:15:35.780
Allow me to explain.

00:15:36.450 --> 00:15:38.760
People shot with one of Cupid's arrows

00:15:38.760 --> 00:15:42.670
are said to fall in love with the 
first thing they see once they're hit.

00:15:42.670 --> 00:15:45.790
But Nina-san was never 
struck with Cupid's arrow.

00:15:46.270 --> 00:15:48.630
Today sure looks like a rare case.

00:15:48.630 --> 00:15:51.600
She was never directly hit,

00:15:51.600 --> 00:15:55.310
but she ate the chocolate 
full of Cupid's love power.

00:15:55.310 --> 00:15:58.100
And the results are clear as day!

00:15:58.680 --> 00:16:03.460
I see. Cupid's arrow is to be feared.

00:16:03.460 --> 00:16:05.800
The arrow's power only 
lasts about a few hours.

00:16:05.800 --> 00:16:08.360
So I think she'll be back 
to normal by tonight.

00:16:08.960 --> 00:16:10.240
Be that as it may,

00:16:10.240 --> 00:16:13.380
it does not change the fact that 
these chocolates are most dangerous.

00:16:13.380 --> 00:16:18.370
I had better dispose of them quickly 
so as to avoid further victims.

00:16:18.370 --> 00:16:24.330
But you tried so hard to make them 
for Karin-chan and Karen-chan.

00:16:24.660 --> 00:16:27.830
It's really too bad, but I've 
no choice in the matter.

00:16:31.330 --> 00:16:33.470
You know it's dangerous, so why?

00:16:35.270 --> 00:16:36.220
Curiosity?

00:16:36.580 --> 00:16:38.880
Spit that out this instant!

00:16:41.960 --> 00:16:45.200
I don't wanna stop. Gimme more.

00:16:48.110 --> 00:16:50.110
No!

00:16:50.980 --> 00:16:53.900
I'm happy we got the special-edition chocolate!

00:16:54.320 --> 00:16:56.950
I hope our mistress is happy with it.

00:16:59.510 --> 00:17:00.200
Goodness.

00:17:00.530 --> 00:17:02.750
There's a good reason for 
what's happened here.

00:17:02.750 --> 00:17:05.710
To begin with, the oven broke down, and then—

00:17:06.280 --> 00:17:09.740
When I look at you,

00:17:09.740 --> 00:17:12.320
my heart won't stop pounding.

00:17:12.320 --> 00:17:13.210
Touch me?

00:17:13.650 --> 00:17:16.220
See? Can't you feel it pounding?

00:17:16.720 --> 00:17:18.510
How about you?

00:17:18.510 --> 00:17:20.050
M-Mahiro-san—

00:17:20.050 --> 00:17:22.470
Call me Hiro-chan.

00:17:22.950 --> 00:17:24.470
H-Hiro-chan—

00:17:24.470 --> 00:17:29.400
Is your heart pounding right here?

00:17:32.340 --> 00:17:35.620
I've never seen our mistress with a 
look on her face like that before.

00:17:35.620 --> 00:17:38.080
We have to protect our mistress!

00:17:38.080 --> 00:17:38.820
Roger!

00:17:41.920 --> 00:17:43.800
Mistress...

00:17:43.800 --> 00:17:45.750
Lick lick.

00:17:46.640 --> 00:17:48.420
Goodness gracious, what should I do?

00:17:48.970 --> 00:17:50.420
Yuko-senpai!

00:17:50.420 --> 00:17:53.840
Please, get that chocolate somewhere safe!

00:17:53.840 --> 00:17:55.220
U-Understood!

00:17:55.220 --> 00:17:56.500
Ya-chan.

00:17:55.220 --> 00:17:57.300
Mistress!

00:17:57.910 --> 00:17:59.930
I wonder where somewhere safe is?

00:18:02.800 --> 00:18:04.440
I'm sorry, I...

00:18:05.100 --> 00:18:06.640
Ow.

00:18:07.400 --> 00:18:08.610
Yuko.

00:18:08.610 --> 00:18:09.760
Sorry. I think you dropped—

00:18:09.760 --> 00:18:10.810
It's—

00:18:10.810 --> 00:18:14.660
I-Is this Valentine's chocolate?

00:18:14.660 --> 00:18:16.530
Yes, it is.

00:18:16.530 --> 00:18:17.860
Thank you, Yuko!

00:18:17.860 --> 00:18:20.370
Um? That isn't...

00:18:17.860 --> 00:18:20.370
Nothing could make me more happy!

00:18:20.700 --> 00:18:23.690
In the history of Mizuki Azuma's life,

00:18:23.690 --> 00:18:26.620
this marks the third happiest 
day to be celebrated.

00:18:26.620 --> 00:18:29.630
First place obviously goes to your birthday.

00:18:29.630 --> 00:18:33.550
And second goes to the day you and I met.

00:18:33.940 --> 00:18:36.480
Finally, my long-cherished 
desire is in my hands.

00:18:33.940 --> 00:18:36.480
Um, about that chocolate...

00:18:36.480 --> 00:18:37.690
Time to enjoy!

00:18:37.690 --> 00:18:39.430
Mizuki! That's—

00:18:42.770 --> 00:18:45.280
Mizuki, are you okay?

00:18:45.280 --> 00:18:46.220
Yuko.

00:18:50.120 --> 00:18:51.400
I have always

00:18:53.080 --> 00:18:55.560
loved you from the bottom of my heart.

00:18:56.300 --> 00:18:58.580
Please accept my feelings.

00:19:05.950 --> 00:19:07.280
Goodness gracious.

00:19:07.280 --> 00:19:09.370
I guess we have Cupid's 
arrow to thank for this.

00:19:09.370 --> 00:19:10.820
Don't worry.

00:19:10.820 --> 00:19:13.290
You'll be back to normal in just a few hours.

00:19:13.290 --> 00:19:15.170
Hmm? What are you talking about?

00:19:15.170 --> 00:19:17.980
Everyone! There's nothing 
to worry about anymore!

00:19:17.980 --> 00:19:20.660
All the dangerous chocolate is gone!

00:19:23.280 --> 00:19:26.320
That was a once in a lifetime 
confession of love.

00:19:40.290 --> 00:19:41.500
Nina-chan.

00:19:43.010 --> 00:19:44.480
What am I doing here?

00:19:44.480 --> 00:19:48.320
You said you wanted to be alone with me.

00:19:49.480 --> 00:19:51.100
I can't believe it!

00:20:02.400 --> 00:20:06.970
Huh? Why are you resting in my lap?

00:20:07.730 --> 00:20:10.200
Y-You've got my hair.

00:20:12.510 --> 00:20:15.660
You're the one who was going on about 
how pretty our mistress's hair was

00:20:15.660 --> 00:20:18.440
and forcing her into that position.

00:20:18.440 --> 00:20:20.990
You can't just conveniently 
forget everything!

00:20:21.290 --> 00:20:24.270
Yeah? It really is pretty.

00:20:24.880 --> 00:20:28.120
Cupid's arrow should have 
lost its effect by now.

00:20:28.120 --> 00:20:29.950
Cut that out this instant!

00:20:36.380 --> 00:20:39.720
I feel as if I just woke up 
from a really long dream.

00:20:40.600 --> 00:20:42.150
I'm tired.

00:20:49.400 --> 00:20:52.100
I forgot to give you this.

00:20:54.690 --> 00:20:56.360
Nina-chan!

00:20:58.210 --> 00:21:00.120
Nina-chan, I love you!

00:21:02.940 --> 00:21:06.950
Episode 11

00:21:02.940 --> 00:21:06.950
Shameful is She 
Who Spurns Chocolate

00:22:45.830 --> 00:22:48.380
Senpai, looks like you've got a 
large haul as usual this year.

00:22:49.060 --> 00:22:52.820
Yeah. Looks like chocolate's 
gonna be my staple for a while.

00:22:56.890 --> 00:22:59.300
Guess it's hard to be that popular.

00:22:59.300 --> 00:23:04.070
Speaking of, have you ever been serious 
about chocolate you've given someone before?

00:23:04.880 --> 00:23:06.880
Sounds like a pain to me.

00:23:06.880 --> 00:23:08.070
How about you?

00:23:08.490 --> 00:23:12.600
I-I have. And I do it every year.

00:23:12.600 --> 00:23:13.910
Yeah?

00:23:18.140 --> 00:23:18.830
Senpai.

00:23:19.690 --> 00:23:20.830
Happy Valentine's.

00:23:20.830 --> 00:23:27.050
Next Episode

00:23:21.650 --> 00:23:24.930
I bet you're just looking 
for triple in return.

00:23:24.930 --> 00:23:27.050
I'm very much looking forward 
to this year's White Day.

00:23:29.410 --> 00:23:30.480
Cheers.
